  {
   "n": "5E-7",
   "titulo": "",
   "partes": [
    {
     "p": "The equality (1) of Notes F is valid for $x \\neq 1,-2$. Therefore, the equality (4)"
    },
    {
     "p": "is also valid only when $x \\neq 1,-2$, since it arises from (1) by multiplication."
    },
    {
     "p": "Why then is it legitimate to substitute $x = 1$ into (4)?"
    }
   ],
   "itens": [],
   "tipo": "aberta",
   "fonte": 0,
   "solucao": [
    {
     "p": "Instead of thinking of (4) as arising from (1) by multiplication by $x-1$, think of it as arising from"
    },
    {
     "p": "$$x - 7 = A(x + 2) + B(x - 1)$$",
     "display": true
    },
    {
     "p": "by division by $x + 2$; since this new equation is valid for all $x$, the line (4) will be valid for $x \\neq -2$, in particular it will be valid for $x = 1$."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": "5E-8",
   "titulo": "",
   "partes": [
    {
     "p": "Express the following as a sum of a polynomial and a proper rational function"
    }
   ],
   "itens": [
    {
     "id": "a",
     "partes": [
      {
       "p": "$\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{2} - 1}$"
      }
     ],
     "tipo": "aberta",
     "solucao": [
      {
       "p": "$\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{2} - 1} = 1 + \\frac{1}{x^{2} - 1}$"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "b",
     "partes": [
      {
       "p": "$\\frac{x^{3}}{x^{2} - 1}$ c) $\\frac{x^{2}}{3x - 1}$"
      }
     ],
     "tipo": "aberta",
     "solucao": [
