  {
   "n": "5E-11",
   "titulo": "",
   "partes": [
    {
     "p": "Solve the differential equation $dy/dx = y(1 - y)$."
    }
   ],
   "itens": [],
   "tipo": "aberta",
   "fonte": 0,
   "solucao": [
    {
     "p": "Separate:"
    },
    {
     "p": "$$\\frac{dy}{y(1 - y)} = dx$$",
     "display": true
    },
    {
     "p": "Expand using partial fractions and integrate"
    },
    {
     "img": "g1/p16-3.png",
     "w": 109,
     "h": 17
    },
    {
     "p": "Hence, ln $y -$ ln($y - 1) = x + c$ Exponentiate:"
    },
    {
     "p": "$$\\frac{y}{y - 1} = e^{x+c} = Ae^{x} (A = e^{c})$$",
     "display": true
    },
    {
     "p": "$$y = \\frac{Ae^{x}}{Ae^{x} - 1}$$",
     "display": true
    },
    {
     "p": "(If you integrated $1/(1 - y)$ to get $-$ ln(1 $- y)$ then you arrive at"
    },
    {
     "p": "$$y = \\frac{Ae^{x}}{Ae^{x} + 1}$$",
     "display": true
    },
    {
     "p": "This is the same family of answers with $A$ and $-A$ traded.)"
    }
   ]
  },
